generator_ts_forms.vlt:40:11: error: a generator must declare its return type
TypeScript allows this (it infers `Generator<T, void, unknown>`); Velt doesn't because the type of the values a generator yields is part of its signature, which is not inferred from its body; write `Generator<T>`, where `T` is the type of the values it yields
generator_ts_forms.vlt:10:13: error: the value of `yield` cannot be used
TypeScript allows this (`yield` evaluates to the argument of the next `next(value)` call); Velt doesn't because `next()` takes no argument, so `yield` has no value; write the `yield` as a statement of its own, and pass values into the generator through its parameters or an object both sides share
generator_ts_forms.vlt:15:13: error: the value of `yield*` cannot be used
TypeScript allows this (`yield*` evaluates to what the inner generator returns); Velt doesn't because generators return no value; write `yield* ...;` as a statement of its own, and yield a last value instead of returning it
generator_ts_forms.vlt:20:7: error: the value of `yield` cannot be used
TypeScript allows this (`yield` evaluates to the argument of the next `next(value)` call); Velt doesn't because `next()` takes no argument, so `yield` has no value; write the `yield` as a statement of its own, and pass values into the generator through its parameters or an object both sides share
generator_ts_forms.vlt:21:8: error: the value of `yield` cannot be used
TypeScript allows this (`yield` evaluates to the argument of the next `next(value)` call); Velt doesn't because `next()` takes no argument, so `yield` has no value; write the `yield` as a statement of its own, and pass values into the generator through its parameters or an object both sides share
generator_ts_forms.vlt:36:11: error: `next()` takes no argument
TypeScript allows this (`next(value)` makes the paused `yield` evaluate to `value`); Velt doesn't because a generator's `yield` has no value; write `next()`, and pass values into the generator through its parameters or an object both sides share
generator_ts_forms.vlt:37:6: error: no method named `throw` found for type `Generator<i64, never>`
TypeScript allows this (`throw(e)` throws `e` at the generator's paused `yield`); Velt doesn't because what a generator throws is checked from its body, and an error thrown in from outside could not be; write `return()` to close the generator (its `finally` blocks run), and throw the error where you call it
generator_ts_forms.vlt:46:10: error: a generator cannot return a value
TypeScript allows this (the value becomes the `value` of the result with `done: true`); Velt doesn't because a finished `IteratorResult` carries no value; write `yield value;` before `return;` to produce a last value
generator_ts_forms.vlt:53:5: error: `yield` cannot be used in a `finally` block
TypeScript allows this; Velt doesn't because a `finally` block also runs when the generator is closed early (`return()`, or dropping it), where it cannot pause; write the `yield` outside the `finally` block (at the end of the `try` block, or after the `try` statement)
generator_ts_forms.vlt:61:11: error: a `finally` block in a generator cannot throw, but this one may throw `Boom`
TypeScript allows this; Velt doesn't because the `finally` block also runs when the generator is closed early (`return()`, or dropping it), where an error has nowhere to go; write a `try`/`catch` inside the `finally` block that handles it
generator_ts_forms.vlt:70:7: error: `break` cannot leave a `finally` block in a generator
TypeScript allows this; Velt doesn't because the `finally` block also runs when the generator is closed early (`return()`, or dropping it), where the generator must finish; write the loop inside the `finally` block, or move the `finally` code out of the loop
